Subject: auth_openid_connect links ext::curl instead of the bare library name "curl"
Error: plugin/auth_openid_connect/src/plugin_openid_connect.cc:18:10: fatal error: curl/curl.h: No such file or directory
Why: LINK_LIBRARIES "curl" is a plain -lcurl (system libcurl). With WITH_CURL=bundled (OpenSSL ruling,
  docs/deviations.md: Wolfi's curl-dev needs the OpenSSL 4 headers) curl's include dir and the bundled static
  library come only from the ext::curl target, which keyring_vault and keyring_kms already link. Build-only fix:
  same curl, linked the way the other curl users in the tree do it.
Upstream: none found (searched the percona-server tree at the pinned tag)
Drop-when: auth_openid_connect links ext::curl upstream, or the recipe goes back to WITH_CURL=system

--- a/plugin/auth_openid_connect/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/plugin/auth_openid_connect/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 
     MYSQL_ADD_PLUGIN(auth_openid_connect
             ${AUTH_OPENID_CONNECT_SOURCES}
-            LINK_LIBRARIES OpenSSL::SSL OpenSSL::Crypto curl
+            LINK_LIBRARIES OpenSSL::SSL OpenSSL::Crypto ext::curl
             SYSTEM_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES "${JWT_CPP_INCLUDE_DIR}"
             MODULE_ONLY MODULE_OUTPUT_NAME "auth_openid_connect"
     )
